# Rust build output and the local cargo home, for every crate under pkgs/ (and the historical ones under
# preliminaries/). Bare directory names, so they match at any depth rather than only at the repo root.
#
# These must never be tracked: they are large (propnix-cli's target/ alone reaches ~1 GB), machine-specific,
# and they would otherwise become part of the flake's source tree — a `nix build` reads the git tree, so a
# tracked target/ makes a package's inputs depend on whatever the last local build left behind. Each crate's
# default.nix filters both names out of `src` as a second line of defence.
#
# Note .gitignore does NOT untrack anything already committed: 827 such files had been tracked under
# pkgs/propnix-launcher/target and pkgs/propnix-prefetch/target and needed `git rm -r --cached` to drop.
target/
.cargo-home/
